# bin/ratchet.mjs starts with a shebang. If git checks it out with CRLF on a
# Windows clone, the kernel on the receiving Linux box reads the interpreter as
# "node\r" and the CLI dies with "bad interpreter". Since releases are packed
# from a fresh clone, that would ship a binary that only breaks on the platform
# it is most likely to run on. Pin every source file to LF regardless of
# core.autocrlf on the machine doing the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything genuinely binary must not be touched at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.tgz binary
